== Threats to Validity <eval-threats>

The threats already known are the following.
- The reference verdicts for part of the randomized nets rest on one tool, LoLA.
- The randomized and parametrized nets are artificial and not necessarily representative of real-world models.
- The sample of MCC models is rather small.
- The results come from a single 10-year-old machine, which may not generalize to other machines.
- The library under test and the evaluation were both written by the same person.
- The memory measurements are not precise because of the overhead of the evaluation harness itself.
